lter -- Test whether the given pattern matches filter\nL2773: ## Synopsis\nL2774: \nL2775:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL2776: \nL2777: \nL2778: ``FcBool `FcConfigAcceptFilter``(FcConfig *`config`, const FcPattern *`font`);`\nL2779: \nL2780: ## Description\nL2781: \nL2782: This triggers a predicate function set by `FcConfigSetFontSetFilter` and return FcTrue if `font` matches something they expect. otherwise FcFalse.\nL2783: \nL2784: ## Since\nL2785: \nL2786: version 2.16.0\nL2787: \nL2788: # FcConfigUptoDate\nL2789: \nL2790: ## Name\nL2791: \nL2792: FcConfigUptoDate -- Check timestamps on config files\nL2793: ## Synopsis\nL2794: \nL2795:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL2796: \nL2797: \nL2798: ``FcBool `FcConfigUptoDate``(FcConfig *`config`);`\nL2799: \nL2800: ## Description\nL2801: \nL2802: Checks all of the files related to `config` and returns whether any of them has been modified since the configuration was created. If `config` is NULL, the current configuration is used.\nL2803: \nL2804: # FcConfigHome\nL2805: \nL2806: ## Name\nL2807: \nL2808: FcConfigHome -- return the current home directory.\nL2809: \nL2810: ## Synopsis\nL2811: \nL2812:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL2813: \nL2814: \nL2815: ``FcChar8 * `FcConfigHome``(void``);`\nL2816: ## Description\nL2817: \nL2818: Return the current user's home directory, if it is available, and if using it is enabled, and NULL otherwise. See also `FcConfigEnableHome`).\nL2819: \nL2820: # FcConfigEnableHome\nL2821: \nL2822: ## Name\nL2823: \nL2824: FcConfigEnableHome -- controls use of the home directory.\nL2825: \nL2826: ## Synopsis\nL2827: \nL2828:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL2829: \nL2830: \nL2831: ``FcBool `FcConfigEnableHome``(FcBool `enable`);`\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFontconfig Developers Reference, Version 2.18.3 (https://fontconfig.pages.freedesktop.org/fontconfig/fontconfig-devel/)\nciteturn6view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn5view2\",\"pattern\":\"FcDirCacheValid\"}); Total lines: 4825\nL3912: Table of Contents\nL3913: 【187†FcFileScan】 -- scan a font file\nL3914: 【188†FcFileIsDir】 -- check whether a file is a directory\nL3915: 【189†FcDirScan】 -- scan a font directory without caching it\nL3916: 【190†FcDirSave】 -- DEPRECATED: formerly used to save a directory cache\nL3917: 【191†FcDirCacheUnlink】 -- Remove all caches related to `dir`\nL3918: 【192†FcDirCacheValid】 -- check directory cache\nL3919: 【193†FcDirCacheLoad】 -- load a directory cache\nL3920: 【194†FcDirCacheRescan】 -- Re-scan a directory cache\nL3921: 【195†FcDirCacheRead】 -- read or construct a directory cache\nL3977: ## Synopsis\nL3978: \nL3979:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL3980: \nL3981: \nL3982: ``FcBool `FcDirSave``(FcFontSet *`set`, FcStrSet *`dirs`, const FcChar8 *`dir`);`\nL3983: \nL3984: ## Description\nL3985: \nL3986: This function now does nothing aside from returning FcFalse. It used to creates the per-directory cache file for `dir` and populates it with the fonts in `set` and subdirectories in `dirs`. All of this functionality is now automatically managed by FcDirCacheLoad and FcDirCacheRead.\nL3987: \nL3988: # FcDirCacheUnlink\nL3989: ## Name\nL3990: \nL3991: FcDirCacheUnlink -- Remove all caches related to `dir`\nL3992: \nL3993: ## Synopsis\nL3994: \nL3995:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL3996: \nL3997: \nL3998: ``FcBool `FcDirCacheUnlink``(const FcChar8 *`dir`, FcConfig *`config`);`\nL3999: \nL4000: ## Description\nL4001: \nL4002: Scans the cache directories in `config`, removing any instances of the cache file for `dir`. Returns FcFalse when some internal error occurs (out of memory, etc). Errors actually unlinking any files are ignored.\nL4003: \nL4004: # FcDirCacheValid\nL4005: \nL4006: ## Name\nL4007: \nL4008: FcDirCacheValid -- check directory cache\nL4009: ## Synopsis\nL4010: \nL4011:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL4012: \nL4013: \nL4014: ``FcBool `FcDirCacheValid``(const FcChar8 *`dir`);`\nL4015: \nL4016: ## Description\nL4017: \nL4018: Returns FcTrue if `dir` has an associated valid cache file, else returns FcFalse\nL4019: \nL4020: # FcDirCacheLoad\nL4021: \nL4022: ## Name\nL4023: \nL4024: FcDirCacheLoad -- load a directory cache\nL4025: \nL4026: ## Synopsis\nL4027: \nL4028:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL4029: \nL4030: \nL4031: ``FcCache * `FcDirCacheLoad``(const FcChar8 *`dir`, FcConfig *`config`, FcChar8 **`cache_file`);`\nL4032: ## Description\nL4033: \nL4034: Loads the cache related to `dir`. If no cache file exists, returns NULL. The name of the cache file is returned in `cache_file`, unless that is NULL. See also FcDirCacheRead.\nL4035: \nL4036: # FcDirCacheRescan\nL4037: \nL4038: ## Name\nL4039: \nL4040: FcDirCacheRescan -- Re-scan a directory cache\nL4041: \nL4042: ## Synopsis\nL4043: \nL4044:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL4045: \nL4046: \nL4047: ``FcCache * `FcDirCacheRescan``(const FcChar8 *`dir`, FcConfig *`config`);`\nL4048: \nL4049: ## Description\nL4050: \nL4051: Re-scan directories only at `dir` and update the cache. returns NULL if failed.\nL4052: ## Since\nL4053: \nL4054: version 2.11.1\nL4055: \nL4056: # FcDirCacheRead\nL4057: \nL4058: ## Name\nL4059: \nL4060: FcDirCacheRead -- read or construct a directory cache\nL4061: \nL4062: ## Synopsis\nL4063: \nL4064:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL4065: \nL4066: \nL4067: ``FcCache * `FcDirCacheRead``(const FcChar8 *`dir`, FcBool `force`, FcConfig *`config`);`\nL4068: \nL4069: ## Description\nL4070: \nL4071: This returns a cache for `dir`. If `force` is FcFalse, then an existing, valid cache file will be used. Otherwise, a new cache will be created by scanning the directory and that returned.\nL4072: \nL4073: # FcDirCacheLoadFile\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFontconfig Developers Reference, Version 2.18.3 (https://fontconfig.pages.freedesktop.org/fontconfig/fontconfig-devel/)\nciteturn6view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn5view2\",\"pattern\":\"FcInitBringUptoDate\"}); Total lines: 4825\nL307: ### Initialization\nL308: \nL309: Table of Contents\nL310: 【4†FcInitLoadConfig】 -- load configuration\nL311: 【5†FcInitLoadConfigAndFonts】 -- load configuration and font data\nL312: 【6†FcInit】 -- initialize fontconfig library\nL313: 【7†FcFini】 -- finalize fontconfig library\nL314: 【8†FcGetVersion】 -- library version number\nL315: 【9†FcInitReinitialize】 -- re-initialize library\nL316: 【10†FcInitBringUptoDate】 -- reload configuration files if needed\nL317: \nL318: These functions provide some control over how the library is initialized.\nL319: \nL320: # FcInitLoadConfig\nL380: ## Description\nL381: \nL382: Frees all data structures allocated by previous calls to fontconfig functions. Fontconfig returns to an uninitialized state, requiring a new call to one of the FcInit functions before any other fontconfig function may be called.\nL383: \nL384: # FcGetVersion\nL385: \nL386: ## Name\nL387: \nL388: FcGetVersion -- library version number\nL389: \nL390: ## Synopsis\nL391: \nL392:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL393: \nL394: \nL395: ``int `FcGetVersion``(void``);`\nL396: \nL397: ## Description\nL398: \nL399: Returns the version number of the library.\nL400: \nL401: # FcInitReinitialize\nL402: ## Name\nL403: \nL404: FcInitReinitialize -- re-initialize library\nL405: \nL406: ## Synopsis\nL407: \nL408:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL409: \nL410: \nL411: ``FcBool `FcInitReinitialize``(void``);`\nL412: \nL413: ## Description\nL414: \nL415: Forces the default configuration file to be reloaded and resets the default configuration. Returns FcFalse if the configuration cannot be reloaded (due to configuration file errors, allocation failures or other issues) and leaves the existing configuration unchanged. Otherwise returns FcTrue.\nL416: \nL417: # FcInitBringUptoDate\nL418: ## Name\nL419: \nL420: FcInitBringUptoDate -- reload configuration files if needed\nL421: \nL422: ## Synopsis\nL423: \nL424:     #include <fontconfig/fontconfig.h>\nL425: \nL426: \nL427: ``FcBool `FcInitBringUptoDate``(void``);`\nL428: \nL429: ## Description\nL430: \nL431: Checks the rescan interval in the default configuration, checking the configuration if the interval has passed and reloading the configuration if when any changes are detected. Returns FcFalse if the configuration cannot be reloaded (see FcInitReinitialize). Otherwise returns FcTrue.\nL432: \nL433: * * *\nL434: ### FcPattern\nL435: Table of Contents\nL436: 【11†FcPatternCreate】 -- Create a pattern\nL437: 【12†FcPatternDuplicate】 -- Copy a pattern\nL438: 【13†FcPatternReference】 -- Increment pattern reference count\nL439: 【14†FcPatternDestroy】 -- Destroy a pattern\nL440: 【15†FcPatternObjectCount】 -- Returns the number of the object\nL441: 【16†FcPatternEqual】 -- Compare patterns\nL442: 【17†FcPatternEqualSubset】 -- Compare portions of patterns\nL443: 【18†FcPatternFilter】 -- Filter the objects of pattern\nL444: 【19†FcPatternHash】 -- Compute a pattern hash value\nL445: 【20†FcPatternAdd】 -- Add a value to a pattern\nL446: 【21†FcPatternAddWeak】 -- Add a value to a pattern with weak binding\nL447: 【22†FcPatternAdd-Type】 -- Add a typed value to a pattern\nL448: 【23†FcPatternGetWithBinding】 -- Return a value with binding from a pattern\nL449: 【24†FcPatternGet】 -- Return a value from a pattern\nL450: 【25†FcPatternGet-Type】 -- Return a typed value from a pattern\nL451: 【26†FcPatternBuild】 -- Create patterns from arguments\nL452: 【27†FcPatternDel】 -- Delete a property from a pattern\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPrecompiled Header and Modules Internals - Clang (https://clang.llvm.org/docs/PCHInternals.html)\nciteturn6view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn4view0\",\"pattern\":\"Validation\"}); Total lines: 349\nL224: Although not explicitly stored as part of the metadata, the predefines buffer is used in the validation of the AST file. The predefines buffer itself contains code generated by the compiler to initialize the preprocessor state according to the current target, platform, and command-line options. For example, the predefines buffer will contain “`#define __STDC__ 1`” when we are compiling C without Microsoft extensions.\nL225: The predefines buffer itself is stored within the 【156†Source Manager Block】, but its contents are verified along with the rest of the metadata.\nL226: A chained PCH file (that is, one that references another PCH) and a module (which may import other modules) have additional metadata containing the list of all AST files that this AST file depends on. Each of those files will be loaded along with this AST file.\nL227: \nL228: For chained precompiled headers, the language options, target architecture and predefines buffer data is taken from the end of the chain, since they have to match anyway.\n"
